{"item_id": "862", "buckets": {"question_type": "free_form", "answer_type": "float", "task": "textbook question answering"}, "score_status": "scored", "correct": false, "extracted": "19.50", "normalized": "19.5", "gold": "10.44", "response": "The horizontal velocity remains constant:\n\n\\[\nv_{0x}=\\frac{D}{t}=\\frac{20.0}{2.50}=8.00\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the launch speed is\n\n\\[\nv_0=\\frac{v_{0x}}{\\cos\\theta_0}\n=\\frac{8.00}{\\cos40.0^\\circ}\n=10.4433\\ \\text{m/s},\n\\]\n\nand its initial vertical component is\n\n\\[\nv_{0y}=v_{0x}\\tan40.0^\\circ=6.7128\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\nAt landing, the velocity components are\n\n\\[\nv_x=8.00\\ \\text{m/s},\\qquad\nv_y=v_{0y}-gt=6.7128-(9.80)(2.50)=-17.7872\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the landing speed is\n\n\\[\nv_f=\\sqrt{v_x^2+v_y^2}\n=\\sqrt{8.00^2+(-17.7872)^2}\n=19.5034\\ \\text{m/s}.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10.44\\ \\text{m/s at launch};\\quad 19.50\\ \\text{m/s at landing}}\n\\]"}
